WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:06.910
On April 16th, 1999, the Raleigh Ripper was
finally brought to justice, after a reign

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:11.449
of terror across the state of North Carolina
that left fourteen women dead.

00:00:11.449 --> 00:00:17.320
The killer’s true identity had been Kevin
Gruber, a local gas station attendant originally

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:22.330
from West Virginia, who was arrested at work
in the early hours of the morning.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:27.580
His face was plastered all over the media
when he was cuffed and dragged in to be questioned

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.079
and processed.

00:00:29.079 --> 00:00:34.280
Like many serial killers, the most frightening
thing about Kevin was the fact that he just

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.570
seemed so...normal.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:41.230
The idea that a person like this could have
committed the atrocities of the Raleigh Ripper

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:45.379
raised a frightening question we all need
to contend with.

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:48.809
What turns a person into a monster?

00:00:48.809 --> 00:00:54.140
This question was particularly prescient for
Dr. James Whitington, a criminal psychologist

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:58.719
tasked with conducting the first official
psychological evaluation on Gruber.

00:00:58.719 --> 00:01:03.769
Ever since the true identity of the killer
had come to light, the case had held a particular

00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:05.680
fascination for him.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:11.670
Mainly because Gruber The Man and Gruber The
Killer seemed to almost be two entirely separate

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:12.670
people.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:18.090
According to all evidence, The Raleigh Ripper
was an insidious, methodical criminal genius.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:24.390
He’d stalked some of his victims - all women
who lived alone - for weeks before striking,

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:29.100
conducting detailed surveillance of their
homes that allowed him to isolate them, bypass

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.610
their security systems, and remove any means
of getting help.

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:38.920
He blocked doors, cut phone lines, and always
selected vulnerable targets.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:43.840
Despite being a seasoned criminal psychologist,
the actual details of Gruber’s crimes had

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:45.440
kept Whitington awake at night.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:49.680
He had a wife and a young son at home, and
the thought of a man like Gruber prowling

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.420
out there made him fear for both of them.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:58.320
This was no thrill killer - He was a sadistic
torturer, who seemed to delight in the pain

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.920
and terror of his prey.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:03.350
He’d chosen victims he could take his time
with.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:08.030
Infiltrated their homes like a gust of cold
air through an open window and slipped out

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:10.119
through darkness like a shadow.

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:12.700
Perfectly controlled crime scenes.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.590
No stray evidence.

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:16.480
Nothing but death left behind.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.599
For months, he’d run circles around the
police.

00:02:19.599 --> 00:02:23.560
Thousands of people who fit the Raleigh Ripper
profile were interviewed.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.819
Sting operations were conducted.

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:29.980
Communities formed neighborhood watches to
keep each other safe from the killer’s next

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:30.980
move.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.700
And none of it did any good.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:39.050
From seasoned detectives to legions of beat
cops, nobody could get the jump on Kevin Gruber.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:44.700
The fact he was even caught came out of pure
chance: A local hiker, Mike Fletcher, just

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:49.500
so happened to hear the screaming coming from
a nearby home in the woods and made the heroic

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:52.409
decision to run in and intervene.

00:02:52.409 --> 00:02:56.920
When he walked in on Gruber committing the
attack, the killer panicked, and fled through

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:57.920
an open window.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:01.439
In his haste, he’d left a partial print
on the window frame.

00:03:01.439 --> 00:03:06.030
That, combined with Mike’s description of
the assailant, was enough to finally link

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:09.469
Kevin to the fourteen murders of the Raleigh
Ripper.

00:03:09.469 --> 00:03:14.819
The problem, from Dr. Whitington’s perspective,
was that, by all accounts, Kevin Gruber seemed

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:16.120
to be an idiot.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:19.159
This was no suave, charismatic Ted Bundy type.

00:03:19.159 --> 00:03:23.770
In all the prior photos and interviews, Kevin
had that deer-in-the-headlights look of a

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.650
man who’s just in way over his head.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:30.409
Dr. Whitington had also pored over Kevin’s
school records.

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:33.099
The only thing he seemed to excel at was being
mediocre.

00:03:33.099 --> 00:03:36.459
He even got held back a year in fifth grade.

00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:40.439
Since graduating high school, he’d been
kicked out by his parents for freeloading,

00:03:40.439 --> 00:03:44.400
and hadn’t been able to consistently hold
down a job for more than eight months.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:49.981
His only prior criminal convictions had been
one drunk and disorderly conduct charge, and

00:03:49.981 --> 00:03:55.359
possession of an ounce of pot back in 1991,
for which he got a suspended sentence due

00:03:55.359 --> 00:03:57.400
to being a minor at the time.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:02.849
It just didn’t make sense to Dr. Whitington
that this man and the diabolically brilliant

00:04:02.849 --> 00:04:08.579
Raleigh Ripper were the same person, despite
all the incontrovertible evidence proving

00:04:08.579 --> 00:04:10.030
it so.

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:15.150
Despite his reservations, he needed to meet
this man, and find out why and how he committed

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:20.770
all these horrific murders, despite being
such an unremarkable individual.

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:25.190
Sitting across from Gruber in the secure interview
chamber, Whitington was once again struck

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:28.290
with how incredibly disappointing he was.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:33.370
Thin and wiry, with glazed-over eyes, messy
hair, and a pathetic tuft of weak stubble

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.510
on his chin.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:38.890
He looked more like Shaggy from Scooby-Doo
than a cold-blooded killer.

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:43.720
His answers to most of Dr. Whitington’s
questions were also insubstantial - with him

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:48.700
often losing his train of thought, or even
needing to ask the psychologist to carefully

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.970
explain the question to him.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:55.660
Most of the time, Gruber tried to make irritating,
slow-motion small talk, concerning everything

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.100
from the weather to movies he enjoyed.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.970
The interview had been utterly worthless.

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:08.280
Until, four hours in, Gruber mentioned something
that awakened a strange memory in Dr. Whitington.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:12.710
He said, “Say, Doc, you remember that TV
show, Bobble the Clown?

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:14.420
I loved that show as a kid.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:15.690
It was like my religion.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:17.060
Your kid ever watch it?”

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:21.560
There were a number of unsettling things about
this, from the fact that, for some reason,

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:26.450
Dr. Whitington could remember something about
Bobble the Clown, to the fact that Kevin Gruber

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:30.390
had no way of knowing that Dr. Whitington
even had a kid.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:35.110
But still, he didn’t let his concern show
and instead asked Gruber what he remembered

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:36.590
about Bobble the Clown.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:39.900
Gruber smiled, and replied: “Bobble taught
me everything I know, Doc.”

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.830
To which Dr. Whitington asked the million-dollar
question, “Like what, Kevin?”

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:47.290
Gruber shrugged and said, “All kinds of
stuff, Doc.

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:49.300
Like how to watch without being seen.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.850
How to jimmy open a window without making
a sound.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:56.600
How to make ‘em hurt real bad without ‘em
dying, see, so you can make it last longer.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:58.620
So it can be more fun.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:02.250
And of course, he taught me to get out without
leaving anything behind.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.710
Bobble made all this possible, Doc.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.650
And he told me all about you, too.

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:07.880
That all this was gonna happen someday.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.660
All good things have to come to an end eventually,
right?

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:13.380
Tell the wife and kid he says hi, by the way.”

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:16.110
Dr. Whitington was astounded.

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:20.500
Gruber seemed to stare vacantly off into space
for a moment, before suddenly claiming that

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:24.370
he had a terrible headache, and he needed
to go back to his cell.

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:28.210
In any other situation, Whitington might have
just written off “Bobble the Clown” as

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:33.760
one of two things - A psychotic delusion,
or a sophisticated psychopath faking a psychotic

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:37.360
delusion in hopes of getting the insanity
plea.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:42.220
Like the Son of Sam Killer, David Berkowitz,
pretending a demonic talking dog possessed

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:45.160
by Satan made him commit all of his murders.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:50.030
But Whitington had heard of this Bobble the
Clown before, and it wasn’t in a scenario

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:53.820
that a gas station clerk like Kevin Gruber
ever would have heard of.

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:58.160
It took half a day of research into his own
archived notes to remember exactly where he’d

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:03.690
heard it before: A child he’d interviewed
almost a decade ago, who’d shoved gasoline

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:08.490
and fireworks through the letterbox of an
old woman’s home, leading to a fire that

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.950
left the woman and her dog dead.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:15.060
When Dr. Whitington interviewed the crying
child about his motives, he’d said that

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:19.890
it wasn’t his fault; Bobble the Clown had
told him to do it on the TV.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:25.060
Given that there were no records of a Bobble
the Clown show ever airing on any local networks,

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:30.010
Whitington had written it off at the time
as the overactive imagination of a very frightened,

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.750
very disturbed young child.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:37.790
That same child would later go into psychiatric
care, before reoffending as a serial arsonist

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.240
upon release.

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:44.920
The last building he ever burned down had
only one occupant: Himself.

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:49.700
Fire investigators would later state that
he just sat there, legs crossed, placidly

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:53.110
waiting for the flames to lick his bones clean.

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:57.390
It was becoming incredibly clear that this
“Bobble the Clown” fantasy - if it were

00:07:57.390 --> 00:08:02.100
even a fantasy at all - seemed to be much
more than an isolated phenomenon.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:06.640
He used his credentials to start exploring
other strange crimes of passion committed

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:11.380
by children and young adults, even asking
some of his friends in the criminal psychology

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:15.820
community - off the record - if they’d ever
heard of such a concept before.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:20.390
Frighteningly, it didn’t take Dr. Whitington
very long at all to hit paydirt.

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:26.330
There was the case of the Orfeo Family Murders
in 1985, out in Arkansas.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:31.590
Nine-year-old Donnie Orfeo had taken his dad’s
rifle out of the cabinet in the dead of night,

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:37.339
and walked room to room, shooting his mother,
father, and two older sisters in their beds.

00:08:37.339 --> 00:08:39.979
Neighbors had heard the gunshots and called
the police.

00:08:39.979 --> 00:08:45.450
By the time they arrived at the scene, the
only survivor was Donnie Orfeo himself, drenched

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:47.940
in blood, sitting in front of the TV.

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:51.089
His hollow eyes stared, zombie-like, into
the static.

00:08:51.089 --> 00:08:53.360
He did not resist arrest.

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:58.189
When Donnie was taken in for questioning,
his emotional responses were cold and flat.

00:08:58.189 --> 00:09:02.670
When he was asked why he murdered his family,
he said that it was because his father told

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:05.380
him he was watching too much TV.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:10.029
His favorite TV character, Bobble the Clown,
had told him that if he murdered his family

00:09:10.029 --> 00:09:14.930
with daddy’s gun, he could watch as much
TV as he liked.

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:18.949
Just reading this, Dr. Whitington could feel
sweat beading on his brow.

00:09:18.949 --> 00:09:22.759
Two cases were a coincidence, but three were
a pattern.

00:09:22.759 --> 00:09:27.620
And oh, how he wished it had stopped at just
three.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:32.189
From four days of searching, he’d discovered
no fewer than seventeen different seemingly

00:09:32.189 --> 00:09:36.529
isolated crimes with mentions of Bobble the
Clown attached to the file.

00:09:36.529 --> 00:09:40.439
A five-year-old boy from New Jersey who’d
drowned his neighbors’ cat in a river with

00:09:40.439 --> 00:09:44.689
a gym bag full of heavy stones told police
that he’d learned the technique from Bobble

00:09:44.689 --> 00:09:45.689
the Clown.

00:09:45.689 --> 00:09:50.180
An eight-year-old girl, arrested for tying
up and torturing her sister with a rusty coat

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:55.940
hanger in Texas, had, of course, gotten the
idea from watching an episode of Bobble the

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:56.940
Clown.

00:09:56.940 --> 00:09:57.940
Murder.

00:09:57.940 --> 00:09:58.940
Assault.

00:09:58.940 --> 00:09:59.940
Vandalism.

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:00.940
Torture.

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:06.320
An extensive, country-wide rap sheet all led
back to that one recurring factor: They all

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:09.170
learned it from watching Bobble the Clown.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:13.899
Dr. Whitington had gotten in contact with
a few friends who knew people in broadcasting.

00:10:13.899 --> 00:10:18.779
While carefully omitting some of the grislier
details, he implored them for any new information

00:10:18.779 --> 00:10:23.420
on whether a TV show with Bobble the Clown
had ever gone out, anywhere.

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:27.600
But despite their best efforts, they didn’t
find any records of Bobble the Clown or any

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.699
similar educational clown shows airing.

00:10:30.699 --> 00:10:33.640
Was it possibly some complex shared hallucination?

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:39.350
Dr. Whitington simultaneously felt burdened
by all this terrifying knowledge, and utterly

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:42.040
powerless to do anything useful with it.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:46.259
If he started blowing the whistle to the media
or his superiors that a spate of horrible

00:10:46.259 --> 00:10:51.240
crimes were all being caused by a violent,
imaginary clown, he’d look just as deranged

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:53.740
as any of the people he’d been studying.

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:58.490
There seemed to be nothing he could do to
stop or help any of this.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:02.720
He returned home that night with a heavy heart,
hanging up his coat.

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:07.190
He needed someone to talk to about all this,
but he couldn’t burden his wife with the

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:12.569
horrors he encountered daily on the job - Much
less a living nightmare like this mysterious

00:11:12.569 --> 00:11:14.170
Bobble The Clown.

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:19.529
As he walked towards the kitchen to pour himself
a stiff drink, he heard strange, jaunty music

00:11:19.529 --> 00:11:21.329
coming from the living room.

00:11:21.329 --> 00:11:27.199
He stepped back, and saw his seven-year-old
son, Ben, watching something on TV.

00:11:27.199 --> 00:11:31.339
As he stepped closer, he could scarcely believe
his eyes.

00:11:31.339 --> 00:11:38.510
Ben entranced, eyes fixed on a dancing, grinning,
animated clown on the screen.

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:43.740
Ben slowly turned his head towards Dr. Whitington,
eyes wide and bulging, and said, “I’ve

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:46.130
been waiting for you to get home, Daddy.

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:48.990
Bobble says he got tired of playing with Kevin.

00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:51.279
He wants to play with us now.”

00:11:51.279 --> 00:11:55.060
Dr. Whitington turned and looked at the clown
on the screen again.

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:58.079
He could swear it was smiling right at him.

00:11:58.079 --> 00:12:03.499
That was the last thing he remembered before
the sudden intense headache, and the ground

00:12:03.499 --> 00:12:05.629
standing up to embrace him.

00:12:05.629 --> 00:12:11.040
When he woke up, he was in bed with his wife,
and neither of them could move - Thanks to

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:14.180
the heavy ropes binding their body to the
frame.

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:17.850
Bobble is very good at teaching children to
tie knots.

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:23.589
They tried to scream, but a shiny flash of
duct tape held both of their mouths closed.

00:12:23.589 --> 00:12:28.889
Dr. Whitington’s eyes swiveled in his head
to Ben, standing at his bedside.

00:12:28.889 --> 00:12:35.399
The boy was holding a kitchen knife, and he
was very eager to show his mom and dad the

00:12:35.399 --> 00:12:39.199
fun new trick Bobble the Clown had taught
him.

00:12:39.199 --> 00:12:46.350
To the SCP Foundation, this terrifying anomalous
TV show is known as SCP-993 - Known to cause

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:50.889
blackouts in adults and violent, antisocial
behavior in children.

00:12:50.889 --> 00:12:55.339
They do their best to keep the broadcasts
contained, but if ever a child in your life

00:12:55.339 --> 00:13:01.579
seems to be acting strangely, perhaps ask
yourself very carefully what they’re watching

00:13:01.579 --> 00:13:03.199
when you’re not around...

00:13:03.199 --> 00:13:08.209
Now go check out “The Secret at the Bottom
of SCP-087 - EXPLAINED” and “Procedure

00:13:08.209 --> 00:13:14.970
110 Montauk REVEALED - Fear Alone - SCP-231
Tale” for more harrowing tales of anomalous

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:15.009
terror!

